WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.932
Hi, I'm Nova!

00:00:02.932 --> 00:00:06.599
Most video generators paint pictures, then guess the 3D.

00:00:06.599 --> 00:00:08.636
GAE generates where geometry lives.

00:00:10.142 --> 00:00:13.619
Generate in a latent a geometry model already reads.

00:00:13.619 --> 00:00:16.323
Decode picture and 3D from that state.

00:00:16.323 --> 00:00:18.255
Geometry never sees the picture.

00:00:20.342 --> 00:00:22.577
Start with Depth Anything 3, frozen.

00:00:22.577 --> 00:00:25.185
It reads frames into four feature levels.

00:00:25.605 --> 00:00:28.079
A codec squeezes those into sixty-four channels.

00:00:28.079 --> 00:00:30.907
Only the channels shrink, never the patch grid.

00:00:31.327 --> 00:00:35.200
A flow model generates in that space: from noise, guided by a

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.427
reference image and camera rays, to one latent per view.

00:00:40.092 --> 00:00:44.408
The raw features' condition number is six point six times ten to

00:00:44.408 --> 00:00:45.847
the sixteenth: numerically singular.

00:00:45.847 --> 00:00:47.286
The latent's is fifty-three.

00:00:48.883 --> 00:00:51.682
To read a latent out, a shared trunk decodes it once.

00:00:52.102 --> 00:00:56.045
One fork, a learned RGB head of two hundred and three million

00:00:56.045 --> 00:00:57.359
parameters, paints the pixels.

00:00:57.779 --> 00:01:01.790
The other rebuilds four feature levels for Depth Anything's frozen head, which

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:03.127
reads depth and rays.

00:01:03.547 --> 00:01:06.224
No path runs from the pixels to the geometry.

00:01:06.224 --> 00:01:09.794
Delete the RGB head and you'd get the same cloud, in grey.

00:01:11.758 --> 00:01:16.417
In the paper's figure, the fork to RGB and geometry happens at the latent.

00:01:16.417 --> 00:01:18.080
The geometry head stays frozen.

00:01:19.442 --> 00:01:21.692
Each point comes from the geometry readout alone.

00:01:22.112 --> 00:01:24.899
Origin: the camera centre, from the decoded ray.

00:01:25.353 --> 00:01:27.003
Plus depth, from the frozen head,

00:01:28.399 --> 00:01:29.731
times the ray's direction.

00:01:29.731 --> 00:01:32.061
The picture only sets each point's colour.

00:01:33.883 --> 00:01:37.487
The authors' render: pictures on the left; on the right, the point

00:01:37.487 --> 00:01:39.290
cloud decoded from the same latents.

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:45.636
Geometry is read, not reconstructed: picture and 3D fork from one latent.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:54.135
To recap: generate where geometry lives, fork two readouts, build points from rays.

00:01:54.555 --> 00:01:56.612
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:56.612 --> 00:01:57.200
I'm Nova.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:57.494
Bye!
